# =============================================================================
# Store — GET BY ID requests (VS Code REST Client) — GET /api/v1/stores/{id} (ADMIN)
# =============================================================================
# Semantics (ticket 0010): a CLOSED store answers 404 by id — closed means
# honest-dead for EVERYONE, including the admin who closed it. The row
# survives at the DB level for audit; the API never shows it.
#
# How to run:
#   1. Start the backend: `docker compose up -d --build` — http://localhost:4000
#   2. Click the "Send Request" CodeLens above any request, IN ORDER, in one
#      sitting (captures are session-scoped).
#
# Prerequisites: the admin persona (see http/store/delete.http header for
# the SQL promotion one-liner).
#
# Notes:
#   - All data is FAKE (devtunde.com emails, Nigerian numbers).
#   - The automated suite for these endpoints: StoreApiTests (src/test/java).
#   - Re-runnable: the manager persona, brand and contact email are minted
#     fresh each run with {{$timestamp}} — no 409 collisions with prior runs.
#   - Access tokens expire after 15 MINUTES. If tokened requests suddenly 401,
#     re-send the SETUP requests from the top (they mint and re-capture).
#   - REST Client captures die on file/VS Code reopen. If you see raw {{...}}
#     template text being sent or sudden 500s, re-send the setup requests
#     from the top — never continue on a dead capture.
#   - Expected codes: 200 found, 400 non-UUID path segment, 401 no/invalid
#     token, 403 non-admin, 404 unknown or closed store, 204 close.
# =============================================================================

@storeUrl = http://localhost:4000/api/v1/stores
@authUrl = http://localhost:4000/api/v1/auth

### 1 — Setup: login the admin persona
# Expected: 200
# @name adminLogin
POST {{authUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 2 — Setup: signup the store manager (minted fresh each run)
# Expected: 201
# @name sellerSignup
POST {{authUrl}}/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Gettable Manager",
  "email": "probe-get-mgr-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348031234584"
}

### 3 — Setup: login the manager
# Expected: 200
# @name sellerLogin
POST {{authUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{sellerSignup.response.body.user.email}}",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 4 — Setup: create a store to fetch (minted brand)
# Expected: 201
# @name createStore
POST {{storeUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "brand": "Gettable Store {{$timestamp}}",
  "storeType": "BRANCH",
  "storeAdminPublicId": "{{sellerLogin.response.body.user.publicId}}",
  "contact": {
    "address": "12 Market Road, Lagos",
    "phone": "08012345678",
    "email": "gettable-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com"
  }
}

### 5 — Fetch by publicId
# Expected: 200 — the minted brand, createdAt/updatedAt present, status ACTIVE
GET {{storeUrl}}/{{createStore.response.body.publicId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 6 — Unknown id
# Expected: 404 — "Store not found"
GET {{storeUrl}}/99999999-9999-9999-9999-999999999999
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 7 — No Authorization header
# Expected: 401
GET {{storeUrl}}/{{createStore.response.body.publicId}}

### 8 — Garbage token
# Expected: 401
GET {{storeUrl}}/{{createStore.response.body.publicId}}
Authorization: Bearer not-a-real-jwt

### 9 — Setup: signup the regular persona (fixed — she never holds a seat)
# Expected: 201 (409 if she already exists — either way the account exists)
# @name regularSignup
POST {{authUrl}}/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Bola Getless",
  "email": "bola.getless@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348031234585"
}

### 10 — Setup: login the regular persona
# Expected: 200
# @name regularLogin
POST {{authUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "bola.getless@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 11 — Fetch as a regular user
# Expected: 403 — by-id reads are admin-only
GET {{storeUrl}}/{{createStore.response.body.publicId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{regularLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 12 — Non-UUID path segment
# Expected: 400, NOT 500 — MethodArgumentTypeMismatchException maps to a
# ProblemDetail naming the offending parameter (fixed in the client-error
# hygiene batch alongside the product module)
GET {{storeUrl}}/not-a-uuid
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 13 — Close the store
# Expected: 204
DELETE {{storeUrl}}/{{createStore.response.body.publicId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 14 — Fetch the closed store
# Expected: 404 — closed = honest-dead; even the admin who closed it cannot
# read the store back through the API
GET {{storeUrl}}/{{createStore.response.body.publicId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
